{
  "task": "M1-131",
  "tree": "build/debug",
  "note": "The coverage hook, the recorder and the shader records (register decisions 544-699, as the task document lists them). The file runs in build/debug, the only tree where every way of stopping runs (decision 698). The recorder's mutants are judged by coverage_recorder. It runs the self-test's program each way it can end, and holds each run to the exit code and the output of the plain program (decisions 634, 636 and 696). The writers' turns are judged by test_writer_turns, with two threads held in step (decision 648). The mutants of the hook's loops in CMakeLists.txt make the build again and rebuild what they change; coverage_hook judges them. The application's shader record and the renderer's callback are judged by shader_record. The readers in the check scripts and in compiled-code.py, and the test driver's shader lists in run-tests.py, mutants-due.py and mutate.py, are judged by their self-tests, run_tests_end_to_end and mutants_due_shaders. Four survive, declared: the recorder's end on a stuck writer (decision 654), the two comparisons of the hook's pointers with the section markers, and the recorder giving up on a second write on the same thread (decision 697). No test reaches them. A program that carries the hook and does not link the recorder does not link at all (decision 626), so that mutant cannot compile and is not here.",
